+ <p class="kb-kicker">Model guide</p>
+ <h1>Enercon E-92</h1>
+ <p class="kb-lead">2.35 MW rated power, 92 m rotor. A larger rotor but a lower rating than the E-82 — that choice explains the whole E-92: it was designed to stay in production for more of the year on low- and medium-wind sites.</p>
+ <h2>Why a larger rotor and a smaller rating?</h2>
+ <p>Rated power is the turbine’s ceiling, reached only in strong enough wind. On a weak-wind site the turbine spends most of its time below it. What counts there is not a high ceiling but useful power in light wind.</p>
+ <p>A larger rotor collects more energy from the same weak wind; a lower rating keeps the generator and power electronics at a point they reach early. The result is an earlier start and a high capacity factor. On a strong-wind site the same choice wastes potential.</p>
+ <h2>Key technical data</h2>
+ <div class="kb-table-scroll"><table>
+  <tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rated power</td><td>2.35 MW</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rotor diameter</td><td>92 m</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Hub height</td><td>78–138 m</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rotor speed</td><td>up to 16 rpm</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Cut-in</td><td>2 m/s</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rated wind speed</td><td>13 m/s</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Drivetrain</td><td>Gearless, direct drive</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Generator</td><td>Synchronous, wound</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Nacelle mass</td><td>64 t</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rotor + hub mass</td><td>41 t</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Wind class</td><td>IEC IIA</td></tr>
+ </table></div>
+ <h2>Drivetrain and systems</h2>
+ <h3>Low speed, high torque</h3>
+ <ul><li>For the same power, lower speed means higher torque; the annular generator and rotor connections carry that load.</li></ul>
+ <h3>Annular generator and heat</h3>
+ <ul><li>A turbine that stays in production for long hours in light wind keeps its generator cooling working constantly; clean air paths are a first-order concern.</li></ul>
+ <h3>Yaw</h3>
+ <ul><li>A larger rotor means a higher moment on the yaw system; lubrication of the adjustment gears and the damping are followed.</li></ul>
+ <h2>E-82 and E-92 (Enercon)</h2>
+ <div class="kb-table-scroll"><table>
+  <tr><th>Item</th><th>E-82 E2</th><th>E-92</th></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rated power</td><td>2.0 / 2.3 MW</td><td>2.35 MW</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rotor diameter</td><td>82 m</td><td>92 m</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Rotor speed</td><td>6–19.5 rpm</td><td>up to 16 rpm</td></tr>
+ </table></div>
+ <h2>Maintenance topics that matter in the field</h2>
+ <ul><li>Generator cooling air paths and filters.</li><li>Pitch emergency supply and connections.</li><li>Yaw adjustment gears and lubrication.</li><li>Blade surface and root connections: periodic visual checks on a long blade.</li></ul>
